# Loaded automatically by Vite/Vitest for `mode: 'test'` (Vitest's default),
# layered on top of .env. Contains no secrets -- just the one override the
# test suite genuinely needs.
#
# rbac.test.ts and services.test.ts (via AuthService.loginAsRoleForTest) rely
# on src/db/dbClient.ts's seeded demo users actually being populated in the
# in-memory store, the same way local development with demo mode on does.
# Since src/db/dbClient.ts now gates that seeding behind a build-time-literal
# check of VITE_ENABLE_DEMO_MODE (see DEMO_SEED_ENABLED in dbClient.ts and
# scripts/check-no-seed-pii-in-bundle.sh -- the whole point is to keep that
# seed data OUT of a real production build), the test run needs this override
# so the same seed data used to being available for tests still is, without
# weakening the production build's guard. VITE_ENABLE_DEMO_MODE="false" in
# .env.example/.env for exactly the opposite reason: production must not seed
# demo/PII data at all.
VITE_ENABLE_DEMO_MODE="true"
